From 29d7055a17415034fb387c05a79566f66f23cdb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gddhd059 <gddhd059@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:27:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] drm/panel: l11a: keep the LK-lit panel prepared/enabled
 in the DRM core

lcm_probe() starts with ctx->prepared and ctx->enabled set because the
bootloader (LK) hands over a panel that is already powered and showing a
picture.  The DRM core keeps its own copy of that state in struct
drm_panel, initialised to false, so drm_panel_unprepare() and
drm_panel_disable() returned early with

  l11a_38_0a_0a_dsc_cmd,lcm 14017000.dsi.1: Skipping unprepare of already unprepared panel
  l11a_38_0a_0a_dsc_cmd,lcm 14017000.dsi.1: Skipping disable of already disabled panel

and never reached lcm_unprepare()/lcm_disable().  A blanking request
therefore only stopped the DSI traffic, and the unblank path replayed a
prepare that had never been paired with a real unprepare, so the panel
stayed lit.

Sync both flags with the hardware that LK switched on.
---
 .../gpu/drm/panel/panel-l11a-38-0a-0a-dsc-cmd.c    | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-l11a-38-0a-0a-dsc-cmd.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-l11a-38-0a-0a-dsc-cmd.c
index 61a18140451f..c1e8288b72e8 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-l11a-38-0a-0a-dsc-cmd.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-l11a-38-0a-0a-dsc-cmd.c
@@ -2654,6 +2654,20 @@ static int lcm_probe(struct mipi_dsi_device *dsi)
 	ctx->panel.funcs = &lcm_drm_funcs;
 	ctx->panel.connector_type = DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_DSI;
 
+	/* The bootloader (LK) hands over a panel that is already powered and
+	 * showing a picture, which is why this driver starts with ctx->prepared
+	 * and ctx->enabled set. The DRM core keeps its own copy of that state in
+	 * drm_panel.prepared/enabled, and it starts out false, so
+	 * drm_panel_unprepare()/drm_panel_disable() returned early with
+	 * "Skipping unprepare of already unprepared panel" /
+	 * "Skipping disable of already disabled panel" and never reached
+	 * lcm_unprepare()/lcm_disable(): the panel kept its power rails and its
+	 * 0x28/0x10 display-off commands were never sent, so blanking left the
+	 * screen lit. Keep both states in sync with the hardware.
+	 */
+	ctx->panel.prepared = true;
+	ctx->panel.enabled = true;
+
 	drm_panel_add(&ctx->panel);
 
 	ret = mipi_dsi_attach(dsi);
-- 
